+---
+name: geno-notes-entries-list
+description: >-
+  List tasks in the active scope, optionally filtered by status. Use when
+  user says /geno-notes-entries-list or wants to see, view, or browse tasks
+  with optional status filter and JSON output.
+argument-hint: "[--status active|backlog|done|abandoned] [--json] [--all] [--global|--project]"
+allowed-tools: "Bash(*) Read(*)"
+license: MIT
+metadata:
+  author: 42euge
+  version: "0.1.0"
+---
+
+# geno-notes-entries-list
+
+List tasks in the active geno-notes scope. Supports status filtering, JSON output, and cross-scope union.
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+geno-notes list [--status active|backlog|done|abandoned] [--json] [--all] [--global|--project]
+```
+
+## Input
+
+`$ARGUMENTS` are passed directly to `geno-notes list`.
+
+## Options
+
+| Flag | Effect |
+|------|--------|
+| `--status S` | Filter by status: active, backlog, done, abandoned |
+| `--json` | Output as JSON array for programmatic use |
+| `--all` | Union both global and project scopes |
+| `--global` | Force global scope |
+| `--project` | Force project scope |
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+geno-notes list
+geno-notes list --status active
+geno-notes list --all --json
+```
+
+## Completion
+
+When this skill finishes, emit a trace:
+
+```bash
+geno-trace emit \
+  --skill geno-notes-entries-list \
+  --status <success|failure|abandoned> \
+  --tool-calls <approximate count> \
+  --errors <count of tool/command errors>
+```
