+
+# geno-notes-site-compile
+
+Compile primary sources into synthesis pages (Karpathy llm-wiki pattern). Dispatches to `geno-notes compile`.
+
+The primary sources (tasks, journal, plans) are the system of record. Synthesis pages are a derived view — persistent, compounding, always rebuildable from primaries.
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+geno-notes compile [--global|--project]
+```
+
+## Input
+
+`$ARGUMENTS` are passed directly to `geno-notes compile`.
+
+## Workflow
+
+1. Run `geno-notes compile` to dump all source material and existing synthesis pages.
+2. Identify distinct topics, entities, themes, and connections.
+3. For each topic, update an existing synthesis page or create a new one under `<scope-dir>/synthesis/<topic-slug>.md`.
+4. Update `<scope-dir>/synthesis/index.md` with a catalog of all synthesis pages.
+5. Log the compile event.
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+geno-notes compile
+geno-notes compile --global
+geno-notes compile --project
+```
+
+## Completion
